WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.634 size:81% position:41%
-Welcome to the show.
-Thanks for having me.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.470 size:88% position:44%
-I feel like I know you.
I feel like I know you

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.105 line:92%
far better than I know you

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:07.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I read you
all of the time.

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:09.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have known Donald Trump
for years.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have covered him
back in his real estate days.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:15.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I want to ask
about last night.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:16.149 line:92%
He talks a lot about unity.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:19.019
And then, at the same time,
says very divisive things.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:23.390 size:84% position:42%
Do you think he's aware
of the contradictions

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.657 line:92%
that exist when he speaks?

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I don't.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:29.095
And I could go into depth
about that if you'd like.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, I mean --
A, I don't think he knows,

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:32.465
and, B, I don't think he cares.
-Yes.

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of the things that he did
during the campaign,

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:37.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
his particular talent
was seeming to take both sides

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.206 size:81% position:41%
of an issue, sometimes
in the same sentence.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And so, last night,

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
you had the soaring rhetoric
at the very beginning.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:46.379
A couple of people compared it
to like "Bohemian Rhapsody."

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
It was like,

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:48.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
here is this part
and then here's that.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:52.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, there was the chorus
of, sort of, unity

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:55.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
and soaring rhetoric
and then we got to immigration

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:57.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
and chain migration
as he talks about all the time

00:00:57.557 --> 00:01:00.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
and limiting the number of
people who can to the country.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:04.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that is where his
administration has rested,

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:07.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
is on those policies.
And he does not see an issue.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You mentioned that thing
about not caring,

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:12.472
I think it is very unlikely.
And maybe you can confirm this.

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did he ever finish
his speaking anywhere

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.141 line:92%
and has a moment of self-doubt?

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:18.278
Or like, "Oh, no, those two
don't make sense together."

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:19.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He might have moments
of self-doubt,

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:22.015
but they are not about
the things that you're thinking.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:22.549 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:25.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
He has moments of self-doubt
about, like, the visuals

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:28.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
or how the scene looked
or whether a particular line

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
sounded good
or he will test things out

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:32.792 size:81% position:41% line:92%
with different people.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.427 line:92%
He's not thinking of it the way

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:35.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're thinking of it.
-Got it.

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:37.330 line:92%
I'm starting to think he and I

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:38.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
don't think the same way
about anything.

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:42.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. No. And I feel like
we arrived at that a while ago

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:44.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you were in
the same room with him

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:45.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the White House
Correspondents' Dinner.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:46.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In 2011. Yeah.
-Sorry.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:48.408
I can't get that out of my head.
-No, we had a different take

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:50.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
on that one, too.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:51.377 size:81% position:41% line:92%
So I want to ask this.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you covered him
for so long,

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:57.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
it does seem like he likes you
at times,

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then at other times,
does not like you.

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:01.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you certainly
have a relationship with him

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
that provides you
a decent amount of access.

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:07.527
And it is true that he has
reached out to sort of criticize

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:11.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
your work at times and gone so
far as to sort of rate it?

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There was one incident
in particular

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:16.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I was in the oval office
last year,

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:20.773
and he was giving me a very hard
time about a number of stories.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he kept saying something
to the effect of

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:23.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You never write fairly
about me."

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:26.646
And I reminded him of a story
I had done about Mar-a-Lago

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:29.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he had thanked me for,
which to be clear,

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:32.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
was not the goal of the story.
And then he said,

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.754
"Oh, that's right. I think
that was about an eight,"

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:36.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
or something like that.
And it was not --

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's not normally what
you hear in response, but, no,

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:40.493
I mean, look,
I've gotten the angry reaction.

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:43.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've gotten the sharpie notes
that an aide

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:44.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
will take a picture of
and send you.

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:48.234
And then I've gotten phone calls
thanking me for a certain story.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
And from each moment
to the next,

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:52.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
it is like the other one
didn't happen.

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:53.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It just starts all over.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:57.110
-Because you've covered him for
so long in his real estate days

00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:01.881 size:81% position:41%
and know, I feel like,
how he used to behave

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:02.916 line:92%
versus how he behaves now,

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:05.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
it does seem like he thought
this job would be easier.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:07.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where do you think
that comes from?

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:09.556 line:92%
-So I think a few things.

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:12.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
A, I don't think he thought
much about running,

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:14.794
what this job would entail
other than running for it.

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:15.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I remember having

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
a conversation with someone
close to him during --

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it was June, maybe,
of 2016.

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:22.669
And I said,
"Does he want to win, just win?

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:25.305
Is that it? Or does he actually
want to be president?"

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:26.239 line:92%
And the person stopped and said,

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.941
"You know,
that's a really good question."

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:30.143 line:92%
And I thought, that is indeed.

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:32.145 line:92%
And I think that was the answer.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.080
And, look, he would be pretty
candid that he didn't spend

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.416
a whole lot of time thinking
about it, he was superstitious.

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:38.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I also think that his view
of executive power

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.220 size:88% position:44% line:92%
was formed in the 1980s.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.955
And he's got this weird,
preserved-in-amber thing.

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:45.391
His cultural references are all
about, like, "Time" Magazine

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
and sort of movies
and celebrities

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:48.561 line:92%
from a certain period of time.

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:51.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that was sort of 1980s
New York,

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:53.766
which was
a pretty corrupt city government

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
where he was
a real estate developer

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:59.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
where laws and regulations
existed to get around.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:00.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
And these were obstacles
that you moved.

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:02.875
And that's, I think, what he
thought it was going to be like.

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.844
It was basically going to be
like mayor of the country.

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:07.547
That is not what it is.
-Turns out that's not how it is.

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is much harder.
-What do you think

00:04:09.716 --> 00:04:10.883 size:81% position:41% line:92%
would bother him more?

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because he talks about
the fake news

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:13.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how he's unfairly treated
in the press.

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
What would bother him more,
a continuation of that,

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:19.325 size:84% position:42%
or if no one ever wrote
another word about him?

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:19.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That.
-Yeah.

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:21.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
Not even a close call.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And do you think
he's aware of that?

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:25.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
And do you think he has a fear
that a day will go by

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
where he's not the --
-Yes, yes, yes.

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:30.903
Even as President,
I still think he has that fear.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:35.608
I had an ex-aide say to me
at one point that he can't go

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:39.078
more than a few days without
seeing his name in the news.

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:41.514
And you will see -- you know,
there is this thing he does.

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:43.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
He loves sitting
in the dining room

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:46.886
next to the oval office
or wherever he's tweeting from.

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:49.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he'll be watching
television, and he'll tweet.

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:51.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then he'll see the news
change.

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:53.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then he is suddenly
on the screen.

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:54.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he loves
that cause and effect.

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:59.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah, he would -- he can't
exist without the media.

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:02.035
-That -- you know, again,
I also think it would be

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:05.238
pretty cool to be able to tweet
and make TV change.

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:06.372 line:92%
Like, I don't begrudge him.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You can't?
-No, it takes hours.

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:09.609 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:12.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I -- So I get the
instantaneous feedback of it.

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:15.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess I wish that
it was more controlled.

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:19.218
-For a different purpose.
-For a different purpose. Yeah.

